{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQcXLHDRdSfs5U9SUPrX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kas3uRJ595HHmhdaU4LXDy","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-976\\docs\\reviews\\wi-976\\024-ADJUDICATE-85fc0a7.md","content":"# WI-976 Done-when sitting at 85fc0a7\n\n## done-when\n\nThe lane changed one group of its Done-when, \"The owner-held step\": three claimed items are replaced by three current ones. Every other item is byte-identical to the claim copy at a51cfae307. The three pairs move the scope: where, when and by what route the owner's SN-036 act is taken, and whether the lane may land before it.\n\nI bless all three moves. Commit 85fc0a7ca's edit implements an owner ruling of 2026-10-25, which `docs/decisions/wi-976.toml` D-023 records in the owner's words. The ruling says why the old route cannot work: the owner took the act in the lane after the re-claim, and the held-rung lane rule (SR-208) refused it, because sitting 016 rules SN-036 MEANING and a held approval lands from a lane only as a CLARITY re-attestation.\n\nThe Context's purpose (\"One sitting, one owner act\") still holds. There is still one owner act, the same snapshot command, still taken by the owner alone. What changes is where and when it is taken, and its carrier stays inside the lane's scope, in the queued owner row the landing must leave. Nothing in the purpose is dropped. The act is not deferred out of the lane's obligations either, since the lane now owes the carrier that makes the act happen, so no successor is owed.\n\n- [MOVED] The owner-held step, its first item -> before: SN-036's re-attestation act, through the needs-only snapshot route, taken attended in the lane, after a re-claim if a headless leg marked the lane -> after: the same act and command, taken on trunk after this lane lands, and the item says why: the held-rung lane rule refuses that act from a lane because the sitting rules SN-036 MEANING -> not the same: the act's place moves from the lane to trunk, and its time from before the landing to after. Blessed. It is the owner's own route (D-023), the act and its authority are unchanged, and the stated reason is a rule this repository enforces (SR-208), not a convenience.\n- [MOVED] The owner-held step, its second item -> before: a headless leg brings the lane to the act and stops, committing the verdict, taking every other act and recording the command and evidence, and \"never takes the act\" -> after: the lane brings its rows to the act, committing the verdict, taking every other act and recording the command and evidence, and \"no session but the owner's takes the act\" -> not the same: the subject widens from a headless leg to the lane, and the prohibition from a headless leg to every session but the owner's. Blessed. It is the same discipline stated for every route, which is stricter rather than looser. The duties to commit, act and record are kept word for word.\n- [MOVED] The owner-held step, its third item -> before: \"The lane does not land before the act\" -> after: \"The lane lands before the act. At the landing, a queued owner row in WI-827's shape carries the act on trunk, citing a pending open item for it.\" The rework clause for a returned SN-036 is kept -> not the same: the landing order reverses, and the lane gains an obligation to leave a queued owner row and a pending open item at the landing. Blessed. The reversal is the direct consequence of the first move, because the act cannot be taken in a lane that may not land first. The gained carrier keeps the act owed and visible on trunk, and the shape it cites exists (`docs/work/queued/WI-827-owner-signs-sn-029-amendment.md`, an owner-signature row of the same kind). A close that leaves no such row, or lands with the act unrecorded as owed, fails the new text, so the obligation is closed.\n\nDONE-WHEN: BLESSED changes=6 digest=sha256:3e6fd0f7989ef765\n\nSITTING: JUDGED kinds=done-when\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1749,"cache_read_input_tokens":837314,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1749},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f031c6a5-ecf0-490f-9890-c7a8a87f92fc","uuid":"30141d3e-90f0-4053-a0a7-7526d8960a68","timestamp":"2026-10-26T09:29:37.848Z","request_id":"req_011CgQcXL164vWChA9LGULWs","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Kas3uRJ595HHmhdaU4LXDy":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-976\\docs\\reviews\\wi-976\\024-ADJUDICATE-85fc0a7.md","content":"# WI-976 Done-when sitting at 85fc0a7\n\n## done-when\n\nThe lane changed one group of its Done-when, \"The owner-held step\": three claimed items are replaced by three current ones. Every other item is byte-identical to the claim copy at a51cfae307. The three pairs move the scope: where, when and by what route the owner's SN-036 act is taken, and whether the lane may land before it.\n\nI bless all three moves. Commit 85fc0a7ca's edit implements an owner ruling of 2026-10-25, which `docs/decisions/wi-976.toml` D-023 records in the owner's words. The ruling says why the old route cannot work: the owner took the act in the lane after the re-claim, and the held-rung lane rule (SR-208) refused it, because sitting 016 rules SN-036 MEANING and a held approval lands from a lane only as a CLARITY re-attestation.\n\nThe Context's purpose (\"One sitting, one owner act\") still holds. There is still one owner act, the same snapshot command, still taken by the owner alone. What changes is where and when it is taken, and its carrier stays inside the lane's scope, in the queued owner row the landing must leave. Nothing in the purpose is dropped. Th